2026-06-02 14:38:47,324 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., a consortium of specialized agents, is pleased to submit this tender proposal for the City of Belval's artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions. Our proposal integrates the contributions of our TechnicalArchitect Agent, SecurityCompliance Agent, Legal Agent, Budget Agent, AIInnovation Agent, CSRSustainability Agent, and ProjectCoordinator Agent. We aim to provide a comprehensive solution that meets the client's requirements while showcasing our expertise in AI, innovation, and sustainability.

# Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks an artificial intelligence solution to improve the efficiency of its administrative services and quality of service rendered to users. The expected solution must provide an intelligent assistance tool for municipal agents, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities. This includes searching for information, helping with drafting letters or answers, and suggesting actions or steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process.

# Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution involves designing a cloud-native architecture using our experience with cloud providers such as OVHcloud, Scaleway, and Outscale (SecNumCloud), all of which are EU-based and SecNumCloud-certified. We will utilize containerization tools like Docker, Kubernetes (K8s), and Helm to ensure high availability and scalability. Our LLM models, including Mistral 7B, LLaMA 3 8B, CamemBERT, and Falcon 7B, will be optimized using quantisation methods like INT8 or INT4 (GPTQ) to achieve a response time of less than 2 seconds. We will integrate our solution with the client's existing systems, including civil-status and town-planning software, EDM, and user directories, using API standards like REST, GraphQL, and SOAP.

Our AIInnovation Agent proposes leveraging our RAG capabilities, including dense vector semantic search, BM25 sparse search, and hybrid search, to provide relevant information to municipal agents. We will also utilize our experience with vector stores like Qdrant, Weaviate, pgvector, and FAISS to enhance the search functionality.

To ensure GDPR compliance, we will guarantee EU-only hosting, prohibit data transfers outside the EU by default, and protect sensitive data through appropriate anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio. Our SecurityCompliance Agent confirms that our data residency is EU-only, and we have a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits transfers outside the EU.

Our Budget Agent estimates an annual cost of approximately 750,000 euros over 4 years, with a total contract value of 3 million euros. We aim to optimize costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected by leveraging our standard daily rates for senior architects, AI engineers, and other necessary roles.

Our CSRSustainability Agent proposes using green hosting partners like OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France, which use 100% renewable energy and have ISO14001 certification. We will also implement digital sobriety practices such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation to reduce GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching to reduce recompute by an estimated 20%, and a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle.

Our ProjectCoordinator Agent will govern the project using established governance tools like RAID logs, decision logs, change request processes, and steering committees. We have experience managing large projects with an average duration of 18 months and a largest project managed worth 4.5 million euros.

# Unaddressed Requirements
While we have addressed most of the client's requirements, there are some aspects that require further clarification or confirmation:
* The specific civil-status and town-planning software, EDM, and user directories used by the client.
* The exact encryption methods for sensitive data.
* The detailed explainability and transparency requirements for AI recommendations.

# Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is confident in its ability to deliver a comprehensive artificial intelligence solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements. Our proposal integrates the expertise of our specialized agents, ensuring a high-quality solution that prioritizes GDPR compliance, innovation, and sustainability. We look forward to the opportunity to discuss our proposal in further detail and explore how we can assist the City of Belval in achieving its digital transformation goals.
